}, {
  "caption": "Figure 2: The framework of our work. Firstly, we construct the searching space for one layer as stated at the left of the figure: we have both transformer architecture hyperparameter as well as graph encoding strategy. Then, we carry out our encoding-aware supernet training method in two stages: on the first stage, we randomly select both architecture hyperparameter (above) and graph encoding strategy (below) and combine them together for supernet as subnet to carry out the training process. While on the second stage, according to using 3 kinds of attention map augmentations or not, we split the supernet into 8 supernets, each inheriting the weight of the supernet before the split, and each training individually adopting random architecture hyperparameter and node attribution augmentations strategy but fixed attention map augmentations strategy. After training 8 supernets separately, we conduct an evolution search on the 8 supernets, evaluating the performance of architecture on its attention map choice’s corresponding supernet. Finally, we obtain our best architecture according to the results on the validation dataset.",
